        "feedback": {
          "grade": "Correct",
          "source_grade": "Correct",
          "result": "Correct",
          "worked_solution": "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total number of pounds of seeds.\n\nSince each of them bought a pound of canary seed and $3$ pounds of sunflower seeds, the number of pounds each person bought is:\n\n$$\n{{1}_{⏟}}_{\\text{canary seeds}}+{{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{sunflower seeds}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person purchased this amount of seeds, and there are $3$ people, we must multiply the number of pounds of seeds by $3.$ Therefore, the total amount of seeds is:\n\n$$\n{{(1+3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{3}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1+3)\\times 3 & =(1+3)\\times 3 \\\\  & =4\\times 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n4\\times 3=12\n$$",
